          "hint": "A cubic with a negative leading coefficient rises on the left and falls on the right. It has opposite end behaviour.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "A cubic has odd degree, so its two ends point in opposite directions.",
              "work": "For large |x|, the leading term −3x³ controls the graph."
            },
            {
              "explain": "Because the leading coefficient is negative, the left end rises and the right end falls.",
              "work": "x → −∞ ⇒ y → +∞;  x → +∞ ⇒ y → −∞"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Only diagram B has this end behaviour and a cubic shape.",
              "work": "Choose Diagram B."
            }
          ],
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "leading coefficient of −3",
              "note": "Use the end behaviour determined by the leading term −3x³."
            }
